.TH LIBRA.A  3R
.UC 4
.SH NAME
System calls with remote access:
.PP
access, chdir, chmod, close, creat, dup, dup2, fchmod, flock,
fork, fstat, fsync, ftruncate, link, lseek, lstat,
mkdir, open, read, readlink, rename, rmdir, stat, symlink,
truncate, umask, unlink, write
.PP
Stdio functions with remote access:
.PP
clearerr, fclose, feof, ferror, fflush, fgetc, fgets, fileno,
fprintf, fputc, fputs, fread, fscanf, fseek, ftell, fwrite,
getc, getchar, gets, getw, printf, putc, putchar, puts, putw,
rewind, scanf, setbuf, setbuffer, setlinebuf, sprintf, sscanf, ungetc
.PP
Other library functions with remote access:
.PP
closedir, opendir, perror, popen, readdir, rewinddir,
scandir, seekdir, telldir
.SH SYNOPSIS
Same as those in UNIX Programmer's Manual (2) and (3).
.SH DESCRIPTION
The functions listed in the first paragraph abive mimic the system calls
for file manipulation.  The semantics are the same as described in
UNIX Programmer's Manual (2), except for accepting remote file names or
remote file descriptors.
.PP
.I Open/creat
a remote file or
.I dup
a remote file descriptor returns a remote file descriptor, which can be
used later on in
.I read, write, lseek, fstat, dup, ...
in the same way as an ordinary file descriptor.
Remote file descriptors are inherited upon
.I fork
(in libra.a),
.I vfork
and
.I exceve
as long as the program to be
.I exceve'd
also uses the remote access versions of the system calls/library functions.
.PP
When an error occurs remotely during a system call, the
.I errno
is copied to the external variable
.I errno
of the client process to indicate the error condition.
.PP
The functions listed in the second and third paragraphs above are
the same as those in libc.a, invoke the functions in the first
paragraph instead of the standard system calls.
.SH RESTRICTIONS
Most other system calls and library functions are not in the
.I libra.a
because they have nothing to do with remote access.
There are a few exceptions which might accept remote file name/descriptor
but whose remote versions are unavailable.  Such system calls include
.I chown, chroot, fchown, fcntl, mknod, mount
and
.I umount.
.SH FILES
/usr/ruan/ra/lib/libra.a
.SH AUTHOR
Zuwang Ruan
.SH "SEE ALSO"
rcsh(1R), commands(1R)
.PP
intro(2), access(2), chdir(2), chmod(2), close(2), creat(2), dup(2),
flock(2), fork(2), fsync(2), link(2), lseek(2), mkdir(2), open(2),
read(2), readlink(2), rename(2), rmdir(2), stat(2), symlink(2),
truncate(2), umask(2), unlink(2), write(2)
.PP
intro(3), directory(3), perror(3), popen(3), scandir(3)
.PP
intro(3S) and the whole section (3S)
.PP
Walter F. Tichy and Zuwang Ruan,
.I "Towards a Distributed File System,"
Proceedings of USENIX 1984 Summer Conference.
